   "alb_idle_timeout_seconds": 60,
   "every_tool_under_the_timeout": true,
   "alb_arm_NOT_DONE_BY_THIS_SEAT": "The authenticated end-to-end call of the thirteen through https://mcp.opalinvest.dev was NOT performed, and this is declared rather than implied. The edge answers an unauthenticated POST /mcp with 401 and www-authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata=.../.well-known/oauth-protected-resource, so the call needs a per-user delegated token; minting or sharing one is forbidden (the gateway's access policy is per-user delegated identity ONLY, app-only or shared identity being stop-the-line). This seat DOES hold a live authenticated MCP connection to that endpoint -- whoami returns a real Opal identity through the ALB -- but its tool catalogue was established BEFORE this deploy and does not refresh without a client reconnect, which this seat cannot force, so the thirteen are not callable on it this session.",
   "what_the_condition_turns_on_and_IS_measured": "whether any tool's work exceeds the 60 s idle timeout. Measured host-side in-region: the slowest of the thirteen is news_for_security at 7.29 s and every other is under 1 s, against a 60 s timeout -- no tool is near it, and no 502/504 occurred. So the STOP arm of the condition (pull a failing tool alone) has nothing to fire on.",
   "owed_by": "a client whose catalogue post-dates this deploy -- naturally 3.0.0_SA_CVO~Z, whose own judgment criteria run through a real client. Raised in the report, not closed here."
  },
  "instrument": {
   "served_read": "g36_served_harness.py under /opt/opal-gateway/.venv/bin/python on i-07dccb1615503ac99, pulled from S3 (Rule 12); host md5 1899403078944fae00771ca108589d03 == the local file, so the bytes that ran are the bytes written",
   "audit_sink": "stubbed: audit.log_call -> _emit -> put_object whenever AUDIT_S3_BUCKET is set, and this order's BOUNDS forbid writing any object. The admission, the tools and the scope seam ran as installed",
   "probe": "synthetic, never written to any store; no object content, .env value, address or tenant/object id printed",
   "a_wrong_probe_was_corrected_and_is_recorded": "the FIRST run read opal_served False for news_search_articles and news_keyword_intelligence, both at 0.00 s with code harvest_bad_argument. That was MY probe, not the tools: each passed the Opal admission and then correctly refused on its own contract, because news_search_articles REQUIRES date_from and date_to and news_keyword_intelligence REQUIRES keyword or date. A wrong-shape call against a real parser returns a real-looking refusal -- the same class as the +00:00 stamp in OG-ap-18. Re-run with a 7-day window inside WINDOW_CAP_DAYS (14) and a keyword: both now serve enveloped answers in 0.88 s and 0.06 s."
  },
